METHOD
For each deterministic arbitrary-factor word, the audit replaces every
square factor Q by q=min(Q,K-Q), constructs the unperiodized line
convolution

  W_hat=product_j tau_(q_j),

and its gradient delta_hat(t)=W_hat(t)-W_hat(t+1).  With L=2K+2 it
forms the paired affine-image shells

  sigma_n(r)=delta_hat(nL+r)
             -delta_hat((n+1)L-r-1),  n>=0.

It verifies exactly that their sum is the finite fusion-square profile.
It then checks shell coordinates, shell anchored currents, pairwise
cross-currents, and every outside-in image suffix

  D_n=sum_(j>=n) sigma_j.

Individual shells and their pairwise cross-currents have exact negative
values, beginning with the word recorded above.  In contrast, all
7,930,793 suffix coordinates and all 53,243,733 suffix anchored-current
coordinates are nonnegative.  These suffix results are bounded evidence
for the outside-in affine-image cone, not an unbounded proof.
Successive suffix-current increments are not nonnegative: the audit
finds 3,421,416 failures, beginning with the exact value recorded above.
Thus an induction cannot demand monotone current growth as each inward
image is added; it must retain the complete remaining suffix payment.
All 1,623,824 adjacent coordinates in proper suffixes are nonincreasing,
and all 1,314,136 tested log-concavity margins are nonnegative.  A
separate high-precision numerical diagnostic finds no negative suffix
fusion eigenvalue.  The shape checks are exact; the spectral check is
diagnostic only.
For the unperiodized ordinary tensor-square multiplicities m_t, all
8,577,872 exact checks of

  (2t+3)m_t >= (2t+1)m_(t+1)

also pass.  This normalized-dimension monotonicity is discovery evidence
for a possible proof of the proper-tail shape, not an unbounded theorem.

